Now, let's create a PHP script to create a call activity for a contact. You'll need to have the contact_id for the contact you want to post the call to. You can get this from the Close.io web app or via the API.

Here's an example PHP script to create a call activity:

```php
<?php

// Replace 'your_api_key' with your Close.io API key
$api_key = 'your_api_key';

// Replace 'contact_id' with the actual contact ID from Close.io
$contact_id = 'contact_id';

// Set up the call data
$data = [
    'contact_id' => $contact_id,
    'type' => 'call',
    'outcome' => 'Connected',
    'duration' => 120, // Duration in seconds
]

// Initialize cURL
$ch = curl_init();

// Set the URL for the API request
curl_setopt($ch, CURLOPT_URL, 'https://api.close.io/api/v1/activity/call/');

// Set up HTTP headers
$headers = [
    'Content-Type: application/json',
    'Authorization: Bearer ' . $api_key,
];

// Set HTTP headers
curl_setopt($ch, CURLOPT_HTTPHEADER, $headers);

// Send JSON data
curl_setopt($ch, CURLOPT_POST, true);
curl_setopt($ch, CURLOPT_POSTFIELDS, json_encode($data));

// Return the response body
curl_setopt($ch, CURLOPT_RETURNTRANSFER, true);

// Execute the API request
$response = curl_exec($ch);

// Check for any cURL errors
