To write a C++ program that implements the bubble sort algorithm with minimal memory usage and error handling, follow the steps below:

First, include the necessary header files and parse the JSON array using a popular library called `nlohmann/json`. If you don't have the library installed, you can find it on GitHub: https://github.com/nlohmann/json.

1. Install nlohmann/json using package manager (if not already installed).
   For example: `vcpkg install nlohmann-json` or other preferred methods.

2. Include the necessary header files in your C++ program:

```cpp
#include <iostream>
#include <vector>
#include <nlohmann/json.hpp> // For JSON parsing

// For convenience, use the 'json' alias
using json = nlohmann::json;
```

3. Implement the bubble sort algorithm function:

```cpp
void bubbleSort(std::vector<int> &arr) {
    int n = arr.size();
    bool swapped;
    for (int i = 0; i < n - 1; i++) {
        swapped = false;
        for (int j = 0; j < n - i - 1; j++) {
            if (arr[j] > arr[j + 1]) {
                std::swap(arr[j], arr[j + 1]);
                swapped = true;
            }
        }
        // If no swap happened, the array is already sorted
        if (!swapped) {
            break;
        }
    }
}
```

4. Write a function to handle JSON input and output:

```cpp
void sortJsonArray(const std::string &inputJson, std::string &outputJson) {
    // Parse JSON input
    json jsonObj = json::parse(inputJson);
    std::vector<int> arr = jsonObj["array"];

    // Apply the bubble sort algorithm
    bubbleSort(arr);

    // Create sorted JSON output
    json sortedJson;
    sortedJson["sortedArray"] = arr;
    outputJson = sortedJson.dump();
}
```

5. Here's a sample `main` function:

```cpp
int main() {
    // JSON input
    std::string inputJson = R"({"array":[5,2,9,1,5,6]})";
    std::string outputJson;

    // Execute sorting
    sortJsonArray(inputJson, outputJson);

    // Display the sorted JSON array
    std::cout << "Sorted JSON array: " << outputJson << std::endl;

    return 0;
}
```

