Yes, there is a way to avoid duplicate environment variables in your Github Actions workflow file. Instead of duplicating certain variables in the `env` section of each job step, you can define variables at the top level of your `yaml` file and reference them in subsequent steps.

First, define all your environment variables at the top level of your `yaml` file, outside any job or step:
```yaml
env:
