You can create a `createSVGElem` function that takes an object as a parameter with properties `type` and `attributes`. The function will create the desired SVG element with the given attributes:

```javascript
function createSVGElem({ type, attributes }) {
  const xmlns = 'http://www.w3.org/2000/svg';
  const elem = document.createElementNS(xmlns, type);

  for (const [key, value] of Object.entries(attributes)) {
    elem.setAttribute(key, value);
  }

  return elem;
}

// Usage:
