To develop a Chrome extension that saves data using JavaScript, you can follow these steps:

1. Create the extension's manifest file:
	* Create a new file called `manifest.json` and add the following content:
```json
{
  "manifest_version": 2,
  "name": "DataSaver",
  "version": "1.0",
  "description": "A simple Chrome extension to save data.",
  "browser_action": {
    "default_popup": "popup.html",
    "default_icon": "icon.png"
  }
}
```
1. Create the popup and background pages:
	* Create a new file called `popup.html`. This will be the page displayed when the user clicks on the extension icon. Add the following content:
```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
  <head>
    <style>
      /* Add some CSS styling here */
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <h1>Data Saver</h1>
    <input type="text" id="dataToSave" placeholder="Enter data to save">
    <button id="saveButton">Save Data</button>
    <script src="popup.js"></script>
  </body>
</html>
```
* Create a new file called `popup.js` and add the following content:
```javascript
document.addEventListener("DOMContentLoaded", function () {
  const saveButton = document.getElementById("saveButton");
  saveButton.addEventListener("click", function () {
    const dataToSave = document.getElementById("dataToSave").value;
    chrome.runtime.sendMessage({ action: "saveData", data: dataToSave });
  });
});
```
* Create a new file called `background.js` and add the following content:
```javascript
chrome.runtime.onMessage.addListener(
  function (message, sender, sendResponse) {
    if (message.action === "saveData") {
      const data = message.data;
      chrome.storage.sync.set({ [dataToSave]: data }, function() {
        chrome.runtime.sendMessage({ saved: true });
      });
    }
  }
);
```
1. Register the background page with the manifest file:
	* Edit the `manifest.json` file to add the background page. Add the following line under the `browser_action` field:
```json
"background": "background.js",
```
1. Add the extension to Chrome:
	* Open Chrome and navigate to `chrome://extensions`. Enable "Developer mode" using the toggle in the top right corner.
	* Click "Load unpacked" and select the folder containing your extension files.
	* Reload the `chrome://extensions` page and enable your extension.

Now, when you click the extension icon, a popup will appear allowing you to enter data to be saved. When you click the "Save Data" button, the data will be saved to `chrome.storage.sync` and a message will be displayed in the popup to indicate the data has been saved.

